4.1.evidence:
counseling/socialization in the form of awareness raising for the wider community down to the smallest community groups (families), especially parents to protect women and children.
activities to disseminate the existence of P2TP2A to be known by everyone in the region through the distribution of brochures, leaflets, pamphlets or bulletin boards so that incidents of violence, exploitation and neglect can be reported as soon as possible and can be handled before reaching the worst level;
training for members who are able to disseminate norms of prohibitions and sanctions to the community;

